    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90861.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 58,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, let's send you back to Syria with your queers for Palestine signs and stuff like that and your purple hair and your your nose rings and all that. Let's just see how long it takes before they throw you off a building just for quote unquote being who God made you to be. Now we're running a little bit short on time today. So I do want to get into something that's tangentially related to the Israel thing. But Mark Wayne, there seems to be a dichotomy with everybody, Republican, independent and Democrat. There's this dichotomy between the support for Israel and support for Ukraine. Everyone seems to have their own nuanced view about whether or not we should do this or that. A lot of the people who would maybe call themselves a MAGA Republican are 100% in support of Israel, but 0% in support of Ukraine. And then there are other conservatives that are kind of split down the middle to where it's like, yes, we need to support Israel no matter what they want to do, but also we need to at least give Ukraine the defensive ability to keep Russia from overtaking their entire country. I got to say, Mark Wayne, I've got my own opinions on it, but it's very confusing. But as a representative of not only me and my state of Oklahoma, but also the United States writ large, how should we view support for both Israel and Ukraine?",
